---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How it works · YOLO Electronics Repair"
  description="How a repair goes at YOLO Electronics Repair in West Sacramento: email first, quote, bench, return. Drop-off by appointment or mail-in."
>
  <div>
    <h1>How it works</h1>
    <p class="sub">EMAIL · QUOTE · BENCH · RETURN</p>
  </div>
  <p class="tag">Four steps. The first one is an email.</p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>The steps</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Email first</h3>
        <p class="note">Write to <a href="mailto:hello@yolorepair.com">hello@yolorepair.com</a>. Say what it is and what it's doing. A model number helps. So does what happened right before it quit.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Get it here</h3>
        <p class="note">Drop it off or mail it in. Both are below.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Quote, then bench</h3>
        <p class="note">You hear the price before any work starts. Nothing gets replaced until you say go.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Get it back</h3>
        <p class="note">Local gear gets picked up. Mail-in gear ships back.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Drop it off</h2>
    <p class="note">For West Sac and the rest of the 916. Drop-off is by appointment, so there's no walk-in counter to find. We set a time by email.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Mail it in</h2>
    <p class="note">For everyone else. Once we've agreed on the repair you get the shipping address by email. Pack it like it's going to be dropped, because it will be.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Not sure it's worth fixing?</h2>
    <p class="note">Ask anyway. <a href="/repairs/">What gets fixed, and what doesn't</a> covers the short version.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
